<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$90.0 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$90.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two issuers sold promissory notes to the Australian market via tender on Thursday.</p>
<p>McDonald's Corp's Australian unit issued A$30 million of early February-dated paper at two basis points over the corresponding bank bill rate. International Business Machines Corp made the larger issue, a A$60 million parcel which sold at three to four basis points over bill.</p>
<p>Traders said physical bank bill flows remained moderate with players still adopting a cautious approach after former Reserve Bank governor Bernie Fraser's comments on Tuesday that the last cut in official interest rates should have been larger.</p>
